# Evidence directories are written at run time by examples and must never be committed.
# (See examples/README.md — the `evidence/` convention.)
**/evidence/
# Some examples emit a SECOND report for a distinct measurement mode, so it can stand beside the first
# rather than overwrite it (iot-timeseries: `evidence/` is the deterministic in-memory mirror the
# committed baseline gates; `evidence-wire/` is the file-backed over-the-wire run that carries the real
# durable-byte evidence). Same rule: generated at run time, never committed.
**/evidence-wire/
